From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:29:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(miniwin): scale retained-mode specular by the light's
 reach

ApplyLighting scaled a positional light's diffuse term by its reach
(range, attenuation and spot cone) but added its specular highlight at
full strength, so an attenuated or half-coned light still left a
full-bright highlight on shiny retained-mode meshes. The immediate-mode
path already scaled both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/miniwin/src/d3drm/backends/software/renderer.cpp b/miniwin/src/d3drm/backends/software/renderer.cpp
index 729c1cb..5b54900 100644
--- a/miniwin/src/d3drm/backends/software/renderer.cpp
+++ b/miniwin/src/d3drm/backends/software/renderer.cpp
@@ -359,7 +359,7 @@ void Direct3DRMSoftwareRenderer::ApplyLighting(
 			if (m_specular) {
 				float dotNH = DotProduct(normal, m_halfway[i]);
 				if (dotNH > 0.0f) {
-					float power = std::pow(dotNH, appearance.shininess);
+					float power = reach * std::pow(dotNH, appearance.shininess);
 					spec.r += power * light.color.r;
 					spec.g += power * light.color.g;
 					spec.b += power * light.color.b;
